# ApexHFT engineering rules

- This is an offline C++20 trading-system simulator, not a live trading system.
- Never connect to brokers, exchanges, or real-money accounts.
- Never run project commands as root; verify `id -u` before implementation.
- Make small, reviewable changes and inspect existing files before editing.
- Preserve deterministic behavior and explicit invariants.
- Use integer ticks and quantities where applicable; avoid floating-point prices.
- Add tests for behavior and edge cases before claiming completion.
- Run the relevant build and tests; report exact results honestly.
- Never fabricate benchmark results or claim unrun tests passed.
- Do not weaken compiler warnings or tests to hide failures.
- Avoid network-fetched build dependencies.
- Do not start a new phase without reviewing the previous phase.
- Record feature status only from executed tests, sanitizers, or measured benchmarks.
